    {
      "id": "anomalies",
      "title": "Worth discussing",
      "narrative": "The one movement worth raising this quarter is the redemption rate on Winback Reactivation, a paid feature. It landed at 48.2% for the week of 6 April, against a usual rate of 61.5%, a drop of about 21.6%. Because Winback sits behind a paid entitlement and the movement runs counter to where the account wants it, it is worth a direct conversation rather than a passing mention.\n\nAcme has already explained the cause themselves. On the 6 May check-in, Priya Raman and Tomas Lindqvist told the account team: \"We cut the winback audience down to ninety days in the first week of April, and honestly we expected the redemption rate to drop. That was the trade.\" [C1] The narrower audience is a deliberate choice on Acme's side, not a signal of campaign fatigue. The conversation worth having is whether the narrower audience is still producing the volume and quality of reactivation Acme wants, now that it has had a full quarter to run.",
